But what's written there is true.

244
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:50,519
Yeah.

245
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:54,732
But you didn't write this
to express Robbie's feelings for me.

246
00:12:57,276 --> 00:13:00,404
You wrote it to express your feelings…

247
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:05,034
for someone else.

248
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:08,913
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:11,415
Jordan.

250
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:15,920
We were together for

251
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:17,546
almost a year.

252
00:13:19,089 --> 00:13:20,341
And I knew.

253
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:22,718
I always knew it was Billy.

254
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:28,390
And I was in denial because…

255
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,268
I don't know.

256
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:35,564
Maybe I was hoping eventually,

257
00:13:36,607 --> 00:13:38,817
you'll learn to love me more
than you love her.

258
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:43,072
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

259
00:13:44,865 --> 00:13:45,699
But…

260
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:46,909
But don't worry.

261
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:50,412
I know we're just friends.

262
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:57,086
But I don't get it.

263
00:13:58,462 --> 00:14:00,089
What's holding you back?

264
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:03,759
Why can't you just be honest with her?

265
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:08,681
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

266
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:13,686
I mean, I'm telling you this
as your friend.

267
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:19,525
Do yourself a favor and talk to Billy.

268
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:23,028
And tell her how much you love her.

269
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:29,076
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:43,549
- [GLASS CLINKS]
- Uh, babe?

271
00:14:43,632 --> 00:14:45,092
- I need to use the restroom.
- Mm.

272
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:46,135
Okay.

273
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:53,934
Mm.

274
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:58,230
What's wrong?

275
00:14:58,314 --> 00:14:59,523
[EXHALES]

276
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:00,649
Okay.

277
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:07,281
I know I wanted Ralph to learn
to stand up to his mother.

278
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:09,575
But now that he has,

279
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:11,869
I feel guilty.

280
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:18,000
I feel like I ruined their relationship.

281
00:15:18,834 --> 00:15:19,877
Don't say that.

282
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,462
You did nothing wrong.

283
00:15:21,545 --> 00:15:24,131
Billy, that's what
I've been telling myself.

284
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:26,175
But I still feel guilty anyway.

285
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:28,928
But, as they say,

286
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:31,305
a parent could never turn
their back on their child.

287
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:35,309
But a child could turn
their back on their parent.

288
00:15:35,392 --> 00:15:37,728
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

289
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:39,772
Do you believe that?

290
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:46,320
Well, it's what I did.

291
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:49,782
But things have changed.

292
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:55,245
You allowed Oliver to talk to his father.

293
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:01,293
Oliver is a different story.

294
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:04,588
I can't say no to that kid.

295
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:06,632
[SIGHS]

296
00:16:06,715 --> 00:16:08,092
But I hope…

297
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,969
I really hope

298
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:12,388
Ralph doesn't ignore his mother forever.

299
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:15,724
I want them to patch things up.
I really do.

300
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:20,813
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

301
00:16:20,896 --> 00:16:23,148
Mm-hmm!

302
00:16:23,232 --> 00:16:24,233
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

303
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:25,734
Thank you.

304
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:30,197
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

305
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,574
- Auntie.
- Hi, Billy.

306
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:34,076
- Mm.
- Mwah!

307
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:40,165
Uh, your brother wanted you to see this.

308
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:44,461
Oh, wow.

309
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:47,464
THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING
YOU'RE THE BEST SISTER IN THE WORLD

310
00:16:47,548 --> 00:16:54,513
I secretly recorded this too,
so I could show it to you.

311
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:55,681
Here.

312
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:02,688
Your father said
he'll never leave you guys again.

313
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:06,692
Have you made your decision, Billy?

314
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:15,159
I gave Oliver what he wanted.

315
00:17:15,242 --> 00:17:16,660
But that's it.

316
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:22,916
Billy, this is going to hurt him.

317
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:27,421
Is it just Oliver who will get hurt?

318
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:29,173
Or you too?

319
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:37,306
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

320
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:39,183
Do you still love him?

321
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:42,352
Even though he lied to you?

322
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,860
[MUSIC TURNS POIGNANT]

323
00:17:49,943 --> 00:17:54,406
He promised he won't leave us anymore?

324
00:17:56,658 --> 00:18:00,496
That is exactly what I'm trying to avoid.

325
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:02,331
Getting Oliver's hopes up

326
00:18:02,414 --> 00:18:05,167
only for him to be
left behind all over again.

327
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:10,297
He needs to walk away.

328
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,965
From you and Oliver.

329
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:18,514
[POIGNANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

330
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:33,570
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

331
00:18:49,753 --> 00:18:50,754
<i>I'm really sorry.</i>

332
00:19:01,098 --> 00:19:06,436
[MARIELA SCREAMING]

333
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:08,981
M-Ma?

334
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:11,191
Ma.

335
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:13,152
Ma?

336
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:15,028
I'm here, Ma.

337
00:19:15,654 --> 00:19:17,281
You're having a bad dream.

338
00:19:17,364 --> 00:19:18,615
Wake up.

339
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:23,495
Are you okay?

340
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:27,082
- Hmm?
- As long as your father

341
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,917
and his mistress are together

342
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:35,090
with that Billy and her little brother,

343
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:39,136
those bastard children…

344
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:44,933
I will never be okay.

345
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:46,685
Never.

346
00:19:46,768 --> 00:19:52,983
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

347
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:04,286
<i>It's already more than enough that</i>
<i>you were given the chance</i>

348
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:05,996
<i>to spend time with Oliver.</i>

349
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:07,873
<i>Billy, please.</i>
<i>I need more time with him.</i>

350
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:11,710
<i>One more week. It's better this way</i>
<i>than to drag this out.</i>

351
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:14,755
<i>Billy is going down.</i>
<i>Mark my words.</i>

352
00:20:14,838 --> 00:20:16,340
<i>I'll tell your wife about it.</i>

353
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:18,675
<i>Hack into LoveLine.</i>

354
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:21,637
<i>Once LoveList is completely ruined,</i>

355
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:25,015
<i>that's when I'll delete</i>
<i>all the pictures.</i>

356
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:25,974
<i>Okay?</i>

357
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:31,813
<i>There has been a huge spike</i>
<i>in the number of subscribers.</i>

358
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:34,483
[BLAIRE] <i>Oh, hi, Sir Fab!</i>
<i>What a surprise!</i>

359
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:36,860
<i>I'd like to take a look at</i>
<i>the LoveLine area.</i>

360
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:38,403
<i>- May I?</i>
<i>- Yes, you may.</i>

361
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:39,947
<i>Feel at home.</i>

362
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:44,451
<i>Sorry, chief. Sir Peter's here.</i>

363
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,537
<i>Huh? You didn't tell me</i>
<i>he was coming today.</i>

364
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:48,997
<i>He just suddenly arrived.</i>

365
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,541
<i>I thought you were expecting him.</i>

366
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:53,085
<i>Hi!</i>

367
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:54,670
- [BILLY] <i>Peter.</i>
- [PETER]<i> Hi!</i>

368
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:55,837
<i>Sorry, I wasn't expecting you.</i>

369
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,089
[PETER] <i>Hi.</i>
